# 0310 = 0309 + RX GPD ring on an uncached alias of its BSS page.
#
# Root cause (docs/125 analysis): the RX GPD ring stayed in cached BSS at
# 16-byte stride, so four GPDs share a 64-byte cache line.  With the ring
# fully armed, the arm/drain dc-civac of one 16-byte GPD writes back the
# whole line and can clobber a neighbour the QMU just updated.  The 1ms
# heartbeat also ran dc civac + HWO scan on the same ring from another
# thread, with no lock.  The TX ring is already on an uncached page
# (rubydmauc=1), which is why TX multi-GPD (M3) was stable while RX
# multi-GPD (M4/M11) intermittently lost one 512-byte packet.
#
# Fix: ruby_rxuc=1 (default) maps an exclusive PAGE_MAX_SHIFT (16 KB) BSS
# struct page (256 B ring + explicit pad, nothing else; aligned 16 KB) as
# an uncached alias: the QMU keeps the same physical ring address that
# worked in 0309, while the CPU never shares a cache line with DMA.  The
# cached alias of the whole page is cleaned once before the UC view is
# used.  RX GPD dc civac is skipped in UC mode; ruby_rxuc=0 keeps the
# cached path for A/B.
# The heartbeat no longer touches the ring: the workloop publishes a
# seqlock snapshot (hwo/cur), and a stuck odd sequence increments
# ruby_rx_snap_bad as the soft ownership assertion.
#
# Payload buffers keep their dc civac: they are separate 16 KB cached
# buffers, page-aligned, with no shared lines.
#
# Default cmdline: config/0310-boot.cmdline (544 B; ruby_rxuc=1 is the
# code default, so the shipped cmdline stays at the 0309 length).
# Acceptance: default 8/8 + M0 512B 60 s + M2 16 KB 60 s no regression.
# Known limit (docs/125): M4/M11 (host transfer spans multiple 512 B RX
# GPDs) still intermittently loses 1x512 B; use matched buffers
# (rxbuf=txgpd >= host transfer size).  Kept as a separate CL-0311 item.
# zero-build A/B: append ruby_rxuc=0 (556 B).
# Banner gate: "RUBY USB: 0310 rxuc=%d".
# patchset: 28ac6272055954bf1495993edeb8b03ffc1069fc15bb1a6bdd15e0cf2641ecc9
#           (291 files, computed locally from baseline-mirror)
KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA=b67a88480fa824e01ca6fc35736cf2d0f302bb33242b8dfb969bd04587e01cde
